<section id="dev-about" class="container section about">
  <div>
    <h2 class="section__title">About</h2>
    <p>I started my career working at an escape room, where I spent years
      solving problems on the fly. I jerry-rigged puzzle mechanics, learned to
      build puzzles that flowed cohesively and carried a storyline, and
      discovered I loved the work of problem-solving. That pulled me toward
      coding.</p>
    <p>After a full-stack development bootcamp in 2019, I worked at GoDaddy as a
      website support specialist, helping customers build the right site for
      their business. I later joined The Moderate Genius and helped build
      Eversend, where I learned how to create features that add value and how to
      think like someone using the product.</p>
    <p>Customer-facing work taught me to bridge what’s technically possible with
      what people actually want, and that’s still how I work: understand the
      problem deeply, explore what’s possible, then build something that holds
      up for the people using it. I’m curious about how things connect and
      comfortable learning whatever a problem needs.</p>
    <p>Based in Minneapolis, open to remote, and looking for my next role.</p>
  </div>
</section>
